_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"31176","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"836","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>What can happen if tooth decay is left untreated in humans?</span></p>","option_1":"Teeth will become whiter","option_2":"Microorganisms may invade the pulp, causing inflammation and infection","option_3":"No conclusive studies have been done on the effect of tooth decay","option_4":"Plaque will dissolve on its own","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Microorganisms may invade the pulp, causing inflammation and infection.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Untreated dental caries progressively destroy the enamel and dentin, eventually reaching the pulp cavity. This allows microorganisms to invade the pulp, causing inflammation (pulpitis) and infection, which can lead to abscess formation if not treated.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject"